<section class="realtime section--panel">
  <div class="wrap realtime__inner">
    <p class="kicker">Real-time</p>
    <h2>One mental model. Different transports.</h2>

    <p class="realtime__body">
      Your business code has one idea — values arriving over time — and in Green Tea that idea is an <code
        >AsyncIterable</code
      >. Declare the transport with a decorator (<code>@Sse</code>, <code>@Ws</code>, <code>@Stream</code>) and
      return the stream; the framework handles framing, backpressure, cleanup and disconnects. Only that one line
      changes between them, and your wire contract is what you declared — never a surprise sprung by a return value.
    </p>

    <p class="realtime__tree">
      <code>AsyncIterable</code> → <code>SSE</code> · <code>NDJSON</code> · <code>WebSocket</code>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
